Harlequin Town was the settlement toward the front of the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]], the most built-up part of the strider, some two roads in a V of low buildings whose insides were hard to read from the street. A clock tower stood at its middle, and off to one side of the tower was a building like a cathedral in stone brick and buttresses and stained glass, which was the town's library.

The library carried no device of the six gods, only an eye among four hands above its doors. Inside was one long open room of shelves and desks, a brazier of reaching spectral hands, a silent reading floor, a wall of fire at the back, and a desk where library goods were borrowed. [[Org/The Harlequins/People/Ocelith|Ocelith]] the curator received readers there, and [[Bestiary/Vermin|zabubs]] fetched the books.

The [[Org/The Harlequins/index|Harlequins]] kept the town in their pinstripes and bell-capped masks. They did not speak to one another; word passed between them in a way like a [[Phenomena/Hearts|Heart's]] skein, and they moved and traded places quickly enough that they were hard to count, near fifty in sight at once. Some worked at construction and shoring up defenses. [[Bestiary/Fiends|Orts]] were kept about as laborers.

The town is gone. Whatever the Harlequins used to move travelers voidward backfired when the Party returned through it, and where the town stood is now an amalgam of purple energy, chunks taken out of the ground with deep violet light filtering up from the holes and strange purple, blue and white masses growing out of them. The old party portal and the doorway to the town's fane opened the way for creatures that crawl out of them still.
